=== task-14 poc-a-dynamic-elf: fail-closed corpus with execution sentinel ===
date: 2026-09-01T09:14:23+08:00 worktree: /home/lain/Projects/esp_study/poc-a-wt HEAD: a302151

--- design decision: serial-upload transport
Chosen: serial-upload (poca fcbegin/fcwr/fcgo) over embedded corpus array.
Justification: (a) proves the parse+verify/admission/relocate pipeline rejects
  ARBITRARY attacker-controlled bytes streamed over the console, not merely
  compiled-in arrays (stronger SEC-004/PLUG-008 evidence); (b) zero firmware
  bloat (15 new fixtures never enter flash); (c) per-fixture sha256 closed
  loop: device re-hashes uploaded bytes, runner asserts == committed file sha
  (stale_state + upload-integrity self-verification); (d) embedded hostile set
  (T5/T6/T7/T8) still driven via poca load for device-side NEGATIVE code
  assertions (consolidated union under one fc_runner manifest).

